Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:03:24 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 432/437] Unified: a file opened with a view that shows nothing
 of the model starts at the home view

Files written by other programs often save no camera (<Camera settings=""/>): the view kept the
default camera a few millimetres across. A point-cloud export of a 20 m room opened as one flat
colour, and the floor's highlight under the mouse turned the whole view blue (status bar
"1.93 mm x 1.01 mm"). Once per document, when its view is first shown after opening: if the model
is a speck or magnified more than 20 times or off screen, ViewHome. A saved camera that shows the
model is kept; a view zoomed in later by the user is not touched. Preference
Mod/Unified/HomeViewWhenModelNotInSight.
